#: artemis/reporting/modules/port_scanner/template_open_port_database.jinja2:2
msgid "The following servers have open database ports:"
msgstr ""

#: artemis/reporting/modules/port_scanner/template_open_port_database.jinja2:14
msgid ""
"This is not a vulnerability and does not mean that anyone can log in to "
"the database - logging in still requires a username and password. "
"Blocking external access to the database provides an additional layer of "
"security - for example, if a backup of a configuration file containing "
"the password is accidentally made public, or if a vulnerability in the "
"application is exploited to read files. Keeping the database port from "
"being publicly accessible makes it significantly harder for attackers to "
"continue an attack."
msgstr ""

#: artemis/reporting/modules/port_scanner/template_open_port_ldap.jinja2:2
msgid "The following servers have open LDAP ports:"
msgstr ""

#: artemis/reporting/modules/port_scanner/template_open_port_ldap.jinja2:14
msgid ""
"We do not recommend LDAP ports to be publicly available - they are "
"frequently exposed by Active Directory domain controllers. Although they "
"can be set up to require correct username and password to login, an "
"attack is possible when the password leaks or is too simple, and the "
"directory may disclose information about users and the internal structure"
" of the organization even to an unauthenticated visitor. The recommended "
"configuration is to make such services available on an internal network "
"only."
msgstr ""

#: artemis/reporting/modules/port_scanner/template_open_port_remote_desktop.jinja2:2
msgid "The following servers have remote desktop ports open:"
msgstr ""

#: artemis/reporting/modules/port_scanner/template_open_port_remote_desktop.jinja2:14
msgid ""
"Remote desktop services shouldn't be publicly available - an attack is "
"possible when one of the accounts has a weak password or when there are "
"vulnerabilities in the remote desktop service. Even if currently such a "
"vulnerability doesn't exist, it may appear in the future, making an "
"attack possible. Historically, remote desktop services were frequently "
"used for ransomware attacks. For remote access, we recommend using a VPN "
"with two factor authentication."
msgstr ""

#: artemis/reporting/modules/port_scanner/template_open_port_smb.jinja2:2
msgid "The following servers have open SMB ports:"
msgstr ""

#: artemis/reporting/modules/port_scanner/template_open_port_smb.jinja2:14
msgid ""
"We do not recommend SMB ports to be publicly available - although they "
"can be set up to require correct username and password to login, an "
"attack is possible when the password leaks or is too simple. When an "
"attacker correctly guesses a password (or takes it from a leak) they can "
"e.g. access or modify files. The recommended configuration is to make "
"such services available on an internal network only."
msgstr ""

#: artemis/reporting/modules/port_scanner/template_open_port_telnet.jinja2:2
msgid "The following servers have open telnet ports:"
msgstr ""

#: artemis/reporting/modules/port_scanner/template_open_port_telnet.jinja2:14
msgid ""
"We do not recommend telnet ports to be publicly available - the password "
"is sent unencrypted and some devices allow anonymous login or login with "
"easy/publicly available passwords. The recommended configuration is to "
"make such services available on an internal network only."
msgstr ""
